WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.520
This is The Spread, your energy
markets briefing for Thursday,

2
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.520
the twenty-second of October.

3
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:10.320
This episode is written with AI,
and read by an AI clone of my voice.

4
00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.920
Two more tankers were hit in the
Gulf, and a drone killed two people

5
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.200
at Saudi Arabia's Shaybah field.

6
00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:20.293
Yet Middle East crude is still
moving at close to pre-war volumes.

7
00:00:20.347 --> 00:00:23.760
The real constraint now is freight,
both for Gulf barrels heading to

8
00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:26.840
Asia and for US diesel heading to Europe.

9
00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:31.120
On the markets. The Oman-Dubai
premium, the main gauge of tightness in

10
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:35.040
Gulf sour crude, has fallen to
four dollars twenty a barrel,

11
00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:38.560
its lowest since the end of
July, according to General Index.

12
00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:42.240
Shipping crude from the Gulf to Asia
now costs more than thirty-seven

13
00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:45.573
dollars a barrel, the
International Energy Agency says.

14
00:00:45.627 --> 00:00:49.840
The EIA's weekly data showed US
commercial crude stocks down about three

15
00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:52.920
million barrels in the week
to the sixteenth of October.

16
00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:56.800
And EU gas storage stood at seventy-four
point six percent full on the

17
00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:57.960
twentieth.

18
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.320
We start in the Gulf, where two tankers
were struck by unidentified projectiles

19
00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.760
on Wednesday, gCaptain reported.

20
00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:06.853
One was near the Strait of Hormuz.

21
00:01:06.907 --> 00:01:09.080
The other was in the
northern Persian Gulf,

22
00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:11.680
further from where earlier
attacks had clustered.

23
00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:15.840
A separate tally reported by Rigzone
logs at least twenty-three incidents

24
00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:19.240
in or near Hormuz in the
first two weeks of October.

25
00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:22.360
At least five of those
involved engine-room damage.

26
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:25.493
That's a fuller count for the
same period than earlier tallies,

27
00:01:25.547 --> 00:01:27.880
not a sign that attacks
are picking up pace.

28
00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:30.360
The physical flows look very different.

29
00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:34.440
According to Bloomberg, Middle East
shipments show little sign of buckling.

30
00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:37.560
That Oman-Dubai premium
is a long way from March,

31
00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:41.400
when it peaked at sixty-five dollars
with Hormuz virtually closed.

32
00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:43.880
Saudi Arabia is a big part of that.

33
00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:47.387
Its August exports rose seven
point nine percent on the month,

34
00:01:47.413 --> 00:01:50.600
to about four point four
five million barrels a day.

35
00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:53.920
That's the highest since March,
according to the Joint Organisations

36
00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:58.320
Data Initiative. At the same time,
production hit a record low of six

37
00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:02.320
point two four million barrels a
day, and refinery runs fell to about

38
00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.133
two point three million.

39
00:02:04.267 --> 00:02:06.187
China is doing much of the buying.

40
00:02:06.213 --> 00:02:08.533
In a note dated the thirteenth of October,

41
00:02:08.587 --> 00:02:12.160
Kpler said Chinese buyers had secured
at least eighty million barrels

42
00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:14.600
of Saudi crude since mid-September.

43
00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:18.400
Onshore stocks there fell by a
record of about one point six million

44
00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:20.120
barrels a day in September.

45
00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:23.600
So the cost hasn't gone away,
it's moved into freight,

46
00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:26.080
now more than five times pre-war levels.

47
00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:30.080
Asian refiners can get sour barrels,
but they're paying for them in the

48
00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:32.800
landed price rather than in the benchmark.

49
00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:36.160
One more Gulf-related
item, and it's unconfirmed.

50
00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:39.600
Reuters, citing a single anonymous source,

51
00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:43.200
says Indian Oil Corporation will
trim its Middle East term share for

52
00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:45.760
the twenty twenty-seven to
twenty-eight fiscal year.

53
00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:49.440
The cut would take it below the
planned forty-seven percent.

54
00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:51.920
The company hasn't confirmed it.

55
00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:56.240
Then there's Shaybah. A drone
hit Aramco's Shaybah field,

56
00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:58.400
which produces one million barrels a day.

57
00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:02.320
Two people were killed and two
injured, according to World Oil.

58
00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:06.480
Saudi Arabia's energy ministry
says operations were unaffected,

59
00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:08.320
and the reports don't name an attacker.

60
00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:12.800
Crude rose on the attack and on
concerns about Gulf embassies,

61
00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:16.240
Rigzone reported, though no
settlement price was given.

62
00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:21.520
Turning to US diesel. The same EIA
report showed distillate stocks up

63
00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:25.120
about one point seven million barrels,
to around one hundred and four

64
00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:29.120
point three million. Gasoline
fell about three million barrels,

65
00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:32.000
and refineries ran at
ninety-three point four percent.

66
00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:36.000
Crude stocks are now three percent
below the five-year average.

67
00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:39.600
That distillate build fits a
read from Kpler on Tuesday.

68
00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:44.320
Freight on the US Gulf Coast to
Europe tanker route is near Worldscale

69
00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:47.360
four hundred, and that, rather than price,

70
00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:49.120
has closed the diesel arbitrage.

71
00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:53.520
Physical differentials swung thirty
dollars a tonne in a single week.

72
00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:57.600
With freight that expensive,
Gulf Coast barrels stay home,

73
00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:00.000
and Europe loses its
swing diesel supplier.

74
00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:04.320
If those rates hold, Northwest
European diesel cracks could firm.

75
00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:09.040
Washington is also tapping the
Northeast home heating oil reserve,

76
00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:11.680
Rigzone reported, though
no volume was given.

77
00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:16.800
And Russia's Novak says the first
Russian diesel cargo for the US sails

78
00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:18.880
today under the Putin-Trump deal.

79
00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:23.840
That's Moscow's account. There's
no US confirmation and no volume.

80
00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:28.320
On Iran sanctions, the US Treasury's
Office of Foreign Assets Control

81
00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:32.720
designated a law firm, shipping agents
and nine vessels accused of moving

82
00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:35.120
Iranian oil, gCaptain reported.

83
00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:39.840
On the same day, it issued general
licences related to both Iran and

84
00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:43.280
Russia. Their terms aren't
in the reports we've seen,

85
00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:46.800
so it's unclear whether they're the
shadow-fleet relief Wright described.

86
00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:51.200
Even if they are, tanker owners and
charterers shouldn't expect much.

87
00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:55.200
Kpler estimated on the fourteenth of
October that only about twenty-four

88
00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:59.440
of one hundred and sixty sanctioned very
large crude carriers could realistically

89
00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:03.840
rejoin trade. That's too few
to ease record freight rates.

90
00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:07.600
In European gas, storage slipped by
four hundredths of a point on the

91
00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:10.400
day, according to Gas
Infrastructure Europe.

92
00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:14.040
It's the first daily fall after
weeks of small injections.

93
00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:17.600
The UK has approved the Jackdaw
field, according to the Department for

94
00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:19.920
Energy Security and Net Zero.

95
00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:22.240
First gas could come
by the end of October,

96
00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:26.320
and at peak it would lift UK
output by about six percent.

97
00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:30.240
Separately, President Macron says
France will receive Qatari liquefied

98
00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:33.413
natural gas this winter.
There are no volumes yet,

99
00:05:33.467 --> 00:05:35.520
and no confirmation from Qatar.

100
00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:36.800
A few more things.

101
00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:40.160
Woodside has resumed commissioning
at Scarborough after protesters were

102
00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:43.440
removed. The project is
ninety-nine percent complete,

103
00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:46.613
with first LNG still on
track for the fourth quarter,

104
00:05:46.747 --> 00:05:49.480
according to Splash twenty-four
seven and World Oil.

105
00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:53.840
And NATO is adding patrol aircraft,
drones and radar in the Black Sea

106
00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:56.693
after the attacks off
Romania and Bulgaria.

107
00:05:56.747 --> 00:06:00.800
What to watch next. Today, whether
that Russian diesel cargo actually

108
00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:02.400
sails for the US.

109
00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:06.000
From tomorrow through the twenty-eighth,
the daily European storage readings

110
00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:08.347
will show whether withdrawals continue.

111
00:06:08.373 --> 00:06:11.573
The next EIA weekly, covering
the week to the twenty-third,

112
00:06:11.627 --> 00:06:13.240
is due on the twenty-eighth.

113
00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:16.720
And the Bureau of Safety and Environmental
Enforcement's shut-in figures

114
00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:19.240
for Hurricane Isaias are still pending.

115
00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:21.640
They've been overdue since the sixteenth.

116
00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:25.200
That's the brief. Sources for everything
you heard are in the show notes.
